      <string id="RealVNC_vncviewer_User_SessionRecordAllowDirOverride_help">The user can override the default storage directory

The default value for this parameter is false.

If you enable this policy setting, the corresponding parameter will be set to TRUE.

If you disable this policy setting, the corresponding parameter will be set to FALSE.

If you do not configure this policy setting, the corresponding parameter will use the default or user-specified value.</string>
      <string id="RealVNC_vncviewer_User_AuthCertificate_help">Hash of the public key to use for authenticating to the remote device, "&lt;auto&gt;" to query for a public key to use, or empty to disable key-based authentication.

The default value for this parameter is "&lt;auto&gt;".

If you enable this policy setting, the corresponding parameter will be set to the value you specify.

If you disable this policy setting or do not configure it, the corresponding parameter will use the default or user-specified value.</string>
      <string id="RealVNC_vncviewer_User_Log_help">Record events in the format &lt;log&gt;:&lt;target&gt;:&lt;level&gt;[,...].

The default value for this parameter is "*:file:30".

If you enable this policy setting, the corresponding parameter will be set to the value you specify.

If you disable this policy setting or do not configure it, the corresponding parameter will use the default or user-specified value.</string>
      <string id="RealVNC_vncviewer_User_Encryption_help">Request that connections either be encrypted (AlwaysMaximum | AlwaysOn | PreferOn), be unencrypted (PreferOff) or let the remote device choose (Server).

The default value for this parameter is "Server".

If you enable this policy setting, the corresponding parameter will be set to the value you specify.

If you disable this policy setting or do not configure it, the corresponding parameter will use the default or user-specified value.</string>
      <string id="RealVNC_vncviewer_Machine_ServerClipboardGraceTime">ServerClipboardGraceTime</string>
      <string id="vncviewer_Machine_category">VNC Viewer Machine Level</string>
      <string id="RealVNC_vncviewer_User_UriSuppressConnectionPrompt">UriSuppressConnectionPrompt</string>
      <string id="RealVNC_vncviewer_User_FullColor">FullColor</string>
      <string id="RealVNC_vncviewer_User_SessionRecordAllowUserControl_help">The user can start and stop session recording as required

The default value for this parameter is true.

If you enable this policy setting, the corresponding parameter will be set to TRUE.

If you disable this policy setting, the corresponding parameter will be set to FALSE.

If you do not configure this policy setting, the corresponding parameter will use the default or user-specified value.</string>
      <string id="RealVNC_vncviewer_User_Monitor_help">The monitor on which to display the application window.

The default value for this parameter is "".

If you enable this policy setting, the corresponding parameter will be set to the value you specify.

If you disable this policy setting or do not configure it, the corresponding parameter will use the default or user-specified value.</string>
      <string id="RealVNC_vncviewer_User_DotWhenNoCursor_help">Show a dot cursor when the remote device has an invisible cursor.

The default value for this parameter is true.

If you enable this policy setting, the corresponding parameter will be set to TRUE.

If you disable this policy setting, the corresponding parameter will be set to FALSE.

If you do not configure this policy setting, the corresponding parameter will use the default or user-specified value.</string>
      <string id="RealVNC_vncviewer_Machine_KeepAliveResponseTimeout_help">The number of seconds to wait for a response to a "keep alive" message, or 0 to wait for the standard transport-level timeout.

The default value for this parameter is "30".

If you enable this policy setting, the corresponding parameter will be set to the value you specify.

If you disable this policy setting or do not configure it, the corresponding parameter will use the default or user-specified value.</string>
      <string id="RealVNC_vncviewer_User_EnableUdpRfb_help">Specify True to attempt Direct UDP with TCP fallback for connections of the form [hostname/address]:port, False to prevent Direct UDP connections, or Force to use Direct UDP without TCP fallback.

The default value for this parameter is "True".

If you enable this policy setting, the corresponding parameter will be set to the value you specify.

If you disable this policy setting or do not configure it, the corresponding parameter will use the default or user-specified value.</string>
      <string id="RealVNC_vncviewer_Machine_ProtocolVersion_60">6.0</string>
      <string id="RealVNC_vncviewer_Machine_EnableUdpRfb">EnableUdpRfb</string>
      <string id="RealVNC_vncviewer_User_PasswordStoreOffer_help">Offer to store passwords when making a connection.

The default value for this parameter is true.

If you enable this policy setting, the corresponding parameter will be set to TRUE.

If you disable this policy setting, the corresponding parameter will be set to FALSE.

If you do not configure this policy setting, the corresponding parameter will use the default or user-specified value.</string>
      <string id="RealVNC_vncviewer_Machine_ToolbarPin_help">Pin the toolbar so that it is always shown (if EnableToolbar is True).

