      <string id="RealVNC_vncviewer_Machine_SessionRecordEncodingFrameRate_help">If non-zero then this is the number of frames per second that are encoded. Otherwise all frames are encoded.

The default value for this parameter is "20".

If you enable this policy setting, the corresponding parameter will be set to the value you specify.

If you disable this policy setting or do not configure it, the corresponding parameter will use the default or user-specified value.</string>
      <string id="RealVNC_vncviewer_Machine_TlsProfile_help">The security strength to enforce when making TLS connections. For 'Normal', TLS 1.2 is mandated, no broken fallback ciphers are allowed, and key strength is checked for security (no SHA-1 or small keys). Selecting 'High' limits cipher choices to AES-256 with no legacy ciphers.

The default value for this parameter is "Normal".

If you enable this policy setting, the corresponding parameter will be set to the value you specify.

If you disable this policy setting or do not configure it, the corresponding parameter will use the default or user-specified value.</string>
