      <string id="RealVNC_vncviewer_User_ConnectInParallel_help">Behavior when multiple servers are specified on the command line.  If true then connect to all servers in parallel.  If false then try connecting to each of the given servers in turn, stopping when one of the connections succeeds.
THIS IS A LEGACY POLICY SETTING. The corresponding parameter applies to older versions of the software. It is ignored by the latest version, and only needs to be set if policy is being deployed to computers running older versions.

The default value for this parameter is false.

If you enable this policy setting, the corresponding parameter will be set to TRUE.

If you disable this policy setting, the corresponding parameter will be set to FALSE.

If you do not configure this policy setting, the corresponding parameter will use the default or user-specified value.</string>
      <string id="RealVNC_vncviewer_User_UseLocalCursor_help">Set this device's mouse cursor to the shape of remote device's mouse cursor.  If false (0) the local cursor will be a dot and the remote device's cursor will be rendered separately.

The default value for this parameter is true.

If you enable this policy setting, the corresponding parameter will be set to TRUE.

If you disable this policy setting, the corresponding parameter will be set to FALSE.

If you do not configure this policy setting, the corresponding parameter will use the default or user-specified value.</string>
      <string id="RealVNC_vncviewer_Machine_Log_help">Record events in the format &lt;log&gt;:&lt;target&gt;:&lt;level&gt;[,...].

The default value for this parameter is "*:file:30".

